-- title:
--   Evaluate one later graph-sketch cell from all predecessors
-- statement:
--   Fix $i<k-1$, state $a<k$ and vertex $v<n$. Suppose the core native invariant holds for layer $i+1$, the index registers contain $i,a,v$, the predecessor counters are empty, and the reverse-ordered label vector of $v$ is loaded. The later-cell program increments $a$ and prepends the framed coefficient array
--   $$
--   \operatorname{denseLayer}(i+2,v,a)
--   $$
--   to the current-layer stack, restoring all other data. For $m$ stored arcs and $W=100(1+n+k)^2$, its charged time is at most
--   $$
--   (C_{\rm pred}+31)n+2\cdot10^6(k+2)^2(W+k+2)2^k+20000(W+1)^2+1000(n+1),
--   $$
--   where $C_{\rm pred}$ is the verified budget for one predecessor vertex and its $k$ previous states. This contract realizes the graph recurrence with the shared sketch signs, rather than independent signs for individual walks.
-- source:
--   T. Koana, Approximate Counting of k-Paths in O*(2^k) Time, STOC 2027 submission #953, October 2026, §3.2 (printed pp. 8–9 / PDF pp. 9–10) and §4.1 (printed p. 9 / PDF p. 10), https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-2/953.pdf. Native implementation: Solutions/LaterCell.lean, line 24; source snapshot SHA-256 ef729e1dbc7f75a251066d01e334bce3ebdc4e2274c19836908fc43a79bf43a4.

